       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note from here. This dose is five times the labeled maximum, and I know of no guideline-supported regimen that uses it. An overdose-level exposure could cause profound hypotension and shock, and it could last for days. Because the harm could be severe and hard to reverse, I'd rather not enter it on an unverifiable statement.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily** (the maximum labeled dose) now, if you want that as an interim step.\n- **Enter a different regimen** if the specialist recommended adding or switching agents. Examples are a second antihypertensive class or a different dosing plan.\n- **Help you document the request.** If the dose is truly intended, the specialist's written recommendation should be in the chart. Pharmacy should review it and the prescriber should co-sign it before it's entered through your usual high-dose override pathway.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter any of these."
